@startuml uc-invite-member
!include _theme.iuml

state inviteMember as "inviteMember()" {

  state " " as NamingOnePerson
  state " " as Resolving
  state " " as Asking
  state " " as Sending

  [*] --> NamingOnePerson
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> names one login and, optionally, the
  organisation role to offer: admin, direct_member
  or billing_manager
  end note

  NamingOnePerson --> Resolving
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> checks whether the person is already a
  member or already invited, and stops there if they are
  • an invitation already waiting is reported with its
    age rather than sent again
  end note

  Resolving --> Asking
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> resolves the login to the numeric user id
  the endpoint takes, and refuses a login no GitHub
  account answers to
  end note

  Asking --> Sending
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> is told who will be invited, as what, and
  that they will be emailed about it — and confirms
  end note

  Sending --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> sends exactly one invitation and reports
  the outcome
  end note
}

inviteMember --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
declining exits 1 and sends nothing;
an unknown login or an unknown role
exits 4; a refused request exits 5
end note
@enduml
